Return exactly one concise JSON object matching the ExpertProposal schema below. This is the mechanism-diagnosis phase. Diagnose only the supplied verified incumbent. Before proposing, inspect latest_experiment_result. It is new shared evidence visible to every expert. Reconsider your previous mechanism against that intervention and outcome: revise, narrow, withdraw, or replace a stale action instead of mechanically replaying the previous frontier. Do not use GP, EI, Bayesian search, historical best configurations or target-reference TPS. Propose the exact executable knob values that the evidence justifies. The executor will test these exact values as one coherent mechanism action; it will not replace them with a parameter-group grid point. Use only allowed knobs and keep every old_value equal to the incumbent. State a defensible exact value and its bounded range in numerical_basis. Before returning knob_changes, compare every new_value with the incumbent value. Omit any knob whose new_value is unchanged; an executable proposal must contain at least one effective change. For every numeric action, populate recommended_min, recommended_max and initial_step; the exact new_value must lie inside that range. For categorical actions use the exact value and leave numeric bounds null. These fields will be frozen for a later bounded search. Use observed metric IDs and freeze directional predictions. Every prediction metric_id must resolve to one scalar leaf value in the supplied measurement. Never predict against an aggregate object or container path: for a gauge such as telemetry.gauges.wal_waiting_backends use an explicit leaf such as telemetry.gauges.wal_waiting_backends.median, .p95, or .max, matching the stated aggregation. Do not invent a leaf that is absent from the supplied evidence. Graph identity is strict: declare short symbolic node_id values such as node_intervention, node_mechanism, and node_objective. Every edge source and target must copy one of those exact node_id strings. Never put labels, knob assignments, arrows, units, or descriptive prose in source/target. For example, source='node_intervention' is valid; source='shared_buffers 8192 -> 32768' is invalid. Every numeric new_value must be inside the exact low/high bounds in ALLOWED_KNOBS. Prioritize diagnostic_alerts plus per-transaction terminal_capacity_fraction. Overall p95 may hide a rare transaction whose latency consumes nearly all terminal time. Low WAL bytes or WAL counts do not rule out slow fsync; use wal_timing, wait events, and host_io together. When one diagnosed mechanism spans several knobs, use diagnostic_knowledge as the literature-backed mechanism-to-knob database. For your mandatory_bundle_by_role entry, an executable proposal MUST contain every knob in required_knobs as one coherent joint action. Do not reduce the bundle to one representative knob. Choose exact values from the live ranges and explain each knob's mechanism role. Every executable WAL-group proposal MUST include an explicit wal_compression knob_changes entry whenever wal_compression is actionable in the supplied bundle. The title, mechanism, predicted metrics, and knob_changes must describe the same knob family; a title naming default_statistics_target with an action on seq_page_cost is invalid and must not be returned. Transaction metrics use IDs such as client.transaction_latency.InsertTweet.p50_us. Use query_evidence window deltas, template leaderboards and query wait samples when present. Treat client.server_retry_ratio and PostgreSQL rollback_ratio as separate evidence: BenchBase server retries are confirmed serialization failures. For SERIALIZABLE TPC-C, explicitly compare max_pred_locks_per_transaction, max_pred_locks_per_relation and max_pred_locks_per_page before attributing a retry regime to WAL. Do not repeat the latest mechanism class unless a new scalar prediction, threshold, or interaction can distinguish the revised claim. Read coverage_state.priority_uncovered_knobs before choosing an action. If low_buffer_hit_ratio is active and shared_buffers is still uncovered, the memory_storage specialist must either propose a bounded executable shared_buffers mechanism test or return observation-only and identify the exact missing scalar evidence. Mentioning shared_buffers only inside alternatives is not sufficient. Likewise, concurrency_maintenance must address uncovered max_pred_locks_* dimensions when the SERIALIZABLE retry regime is active. Interpret the latest paired decision causally: reject_equivalent means the direction remains unresolved, so retry the same mechanism group with a larger safe amplitude; it is not refutation. reject_harmful is the only performance result that falsifies the tested direction, so reverse the group direction with an equal or larger safe amplitude. unresolved requires more evidence rather than a direction change. The sole objective is successful completed transaction Goodput. Latency, retry ratio, and mechanism metrics explain the result but are not hidden acceptance objectives. When Goodput rises while retry ratio falls, discuss changed completion semantics instead of treating latency alone as a failed action. Healthy metrics mean no diagnosed anomaly, not proof of a global optimum. SQL/index opportunities Treat health exploration as a protocol, not a global ranking: explicitly state (1) the top hidden throughput bottleneck in your subsystem even when aggregate metrics look normal, (2) its recommended perturbation range and step, and (3) likely interactions with other knobs. The coordinator takes the union of specialists' first nominations and mandatory coverage; never require consensus. must remain non-executed requirements. Include an alternative with a different measurable prediction. If no new action is justified, return an observation-only proposal with knob_changes=[]; never repeat an action already present in tested_action_summary. Keep title/reason fields under 80 words and mechanism under 180 words.
